>>we have the following problem:
>>  we wan't to include an ascii file into dec-write, so far no problem
>>  but the text file should contain some primitive formatting commands
>>  for example to print some words bold or italic.
>>Is there a simple way to do this, may be some public domain converter
>>from text to ddif, or is there a document describing the ddif format ?

DECwrite includes a text converter in its kit, which allows 
you to import text files into DECWrite. The text converter 
does not allow for formatting commands such as bolding, however.

One option might be to mark up your text document using, for example, roff 
or SGML and import from these formats into DECwrite. (This would require 
the use of the Digital CDA Converter Library.)

Marking up your document using roff would be very simple.

The DEC standard 078 specifies the DDIF format. Other documentation is also available, for example, the CDA Guide to Writing Converters.

-Tom.


