To users of DEC-WRITE on the VAX/VMS system:

I was encountering problems with the "link to picture" command.  After invoking
the command, the picture (500 block *.eps file) would only be partly created.
The following error message appeared:
    "Timer expired.   Note:  A bad postscript file can cause this."

After contacting DECWRITE they suggested I try re-setting the timer as follows:
     define/job write_epstimout 360
The 360 refers to seconds.  Same error message after 30 seconds or so.

ECS consultant here at UMASS finally figured it out, the command is:
     ass/sys/exec 10000 write_epstimout
I imagine this will give me 10000 seconds before the timer expires.  So far
I haven't encountered any problems.

