The VMS version of /dev/null is NLA0:.  On writes, it immediately
completes the operation successfully, and on reads returns success
with length of zero.

The equivalent of /dev/groundplug is GPA0:, implimented as follows:
  define/system/exec GPA0 NLA0

or you can use:
  define/system/exec GROUNDPLUG1 NLA0

:-)

happy bit-bucketing

