  Unfortunately, DEC doesn't count "worthy causes" as a valid reason for 
copying the media. If you can get a letter from your DEC office requesting
that someone provide you with copies of the media, you'd get better respon-
ses. Note that even in the DECUS South Pacific area, where "hobbyist use"
PDP-11 software licenses are NZ $25, you still have to buy the media and
doc.

  In theory, PDP-11 licenses can be transfered the same way as the VMS oper-
ating system (when buying a CPU, the license can be transfered after paying
a US $300 fee). After DEC approves the transfer, you are allowed to take the
media and documentation from the seller as well. Of course, that requres that
you buy another CPU that has the license, media, and doc that you want, and
the DEC policy may differ in your area.

  If you are going to move from V8 to V10.1 (the current and final release),
you really want the documentation as well, because things have *really* changed
in between.

