Regarding UNIX/X11 - you can get the Alpha PC 150 (same machine as the
DEC 2000/300) with Digital OSF/1 for Alpha AXP.  Version 1.3B of OSF/1 includes
X Windows support for the Compaq QVISION graphics card.  It is marketed
as a "server" rather than a workstation I guess because the X performance
is not up to HX/TURBOchannel levels.  I find it perfectly satisfactory
and you may too.  OSF/1 supports both BSD and SYSV styles of Unix.
Except for the slow EISA bus that limits graphics performance, the machine
disk and compute-wise is quite zippy.  (The standard machine runs the
21064 CPU at 150 MHz, but there was a demo system running at COMDEX
with a 21064A at 320 MHz (!))

Regarding sound, the Cambridge Research Lab has a version of our
AudioFile (oops, I mean AF) audio software that supports the Microsoft Sound
Board plugged into a DEC 2000/300 Alpha PC, running OSF/1.  Works fine at up 
to 48 KHz sampling rates.  We expect to make this support available 
Real Soon Now.

