I'm very surprised that you haven't been FLOODED with responses to
your question.  I have seen none to date, so I will reply.

The device you are after is NLA0:, which can be abbreviated to NL:
(this abbreviation is the same for any device, the controller letter
"A" and unit number "0" are assumed if omitted).  This is a very fast
device !!!! :-)

If you attempt to read from NL: it will immediately return an end-of-file
(^Z, ascii 26), and if you write to it, it will soak up data as fast as
you can write to it !!

I often suggest to users that if they have any complaints, they should
direct them to NL: !!!

I suppose thousands of others will reply to your question, probably
without noticing that I have to.  Groan !!

