All Alpha AXP systems, including the low end, are available with DEC OSF/1,
Digital's UNIX offering.  All systems with some type of frame buffer,
including the Alpha PC, are available with X11 and MOTIF.

The 3000 series all have built-in sound capabilities.  You have to grab a
copy of AudioFile (it may be on the freeware disk - it's definitely available
on gatekeeper.dec.com for anonymous FTP).  AudioFile is pretty cool - it's a
client/server sound setup, modeled very much after X11.  The versions on 
gatekeeper also support sun and SGI.

I don't know if the PC has any audio hardware - I don't think so.  Of course,
since the Alpha PC is an EISA machine, it would be perfectly possible to write
an AudioFile driver for a Soundblaster Pro or something similar.

