|> word processor formats (like WordPerfect, or Microsoft Word)? I have
|> the CDA converter kit installed; is that it, by any chance?

  The CDA converters are the tools to use.  In early versions of DECwrite,
you could export your document directly from a DECwrite session into any of
the formats supported by available CDA converters (available on your system).
Try the File menu or just HELP CONVERT.  Again, this is from memory and may
be out of date.

  On the indexing stuff, I recall that the interaction was set up so that you
could do something like select the word you wanted to index, then invoke the
index dialog and the dialog would be set to index the selected word.  It's been
a number of years, but that's the way I recall implementing it.  I would hope
that it has been improved since V1.0.

  Yes, I was on the V1.0 DECwrite development team. And, contrary to popular
belief, there *were* V1 bugs. :)

