In article <2cgpfa$p28@slab.mtholyoke.edu>, jbotz@mtholyoke.edu (Jurgen Botz) writes:

>Are the DEC rz28 and dsp3210 the same drive?  If not, how are they
>different?  Thanks...

I think the HDA is the same and wouldn't be surprised if the
PC board wasn't pretty much the same.  The differences are
in the microcode provided by the different vendors of the
DSP3210 (we just make them...).  Since we are an OEM we
make whatever changes to the base microcode a particular
vendor wants and that's what they get.  As for particular
differences, you'll have to ask the vendors.

Another thing to consider is that the microcode for the
drive is always evolving with performance, integrity and
reliability improvments going in.

