This is a good story!  -Two- VAX-11/780s in a garage!  However,
being the, ahem, "lout" that I am, I _have_ to try and top this.

My first-ever VAX that I owned was a VAX-11/750.  Back when I was living
in an apartment.  On the third floor.  With no elevator.

When the carrier came to deliver my new toy, the landlady looked at the
18-wheeler truck pulling into the apartment complex and exclaimed, "what the
h-ll did Bill buy now?!"   The driver's exclamation was even more erudite
when he found out that the stuff had to go up three flights of stairs, and
he didn't bring any stair crawlers.  <heh, heh, heh>

I had asked a friend of mine to open up the apartment and be there to sign
the delivery receipts.  When he got there, they had just finished delivering
the equipment.  It took the driver, my land-lord-, and two of his workers
about two hours to push everything up the stairs.  What did they deliver?
Only what every growing VAXen needs.  To wit:

	1 - VAX-11/750
	1 - Cabinet of (3) RA60 disk drives
	1 - TU80 tape drive
	1 - Data Products B900 band printer
	1 - Power Conditioner

Plus the usual assortment of cables, terminals servers, Ethernet 
transceivers, disk packs, etc.

One of my neighbors commented later that he was there during the delivery, 
and that the printer took a tumble down one of the flights of stairs.  Made 
a racket that would awaken the dead, he said.  Interestingly enough, when I 
plugged it in, the printer worked just fine.  Sort of reminds me of the 
Samsonsite commercial of the ape throwing the luggage around.

One final anecdote to finish this story off:  During this time, my 
ladyfriend was going through therapy because of a horrific trauma she had 
undergone.  During the sessions, she remarked to the therapist about how she 
had "this friend who's installing a mainframe computer in his apartment."  
The therapist looked disdainfully at her and said, "Really now, Mary.  
You've got to get over these imaginary friends of yours.  *Nobody* puts a 
mainframe computer in an apartment."  After she related this to me, I 
invited her over to take pictures of me with my new VAX.  She had fun 
showing the photo album to the shrink on her next visit.  Chalk one up for 
the mentally ill!  ;-)

Okay, who's next?

