In article <2ch4t3$a1j@nic.lth.se>, ph@loglady.df.lth.se (Per Hall) writes:
> Problem description:
> At spin up, the drive gives the following error:
> 
> %RA81-TEST: SUBTEST:0A  ERROR:3A  UNIT:000
> %RA81-FRU-MICRO.SDI-CONTROLER
> 
> The error code is repeated several times.
> Any help is appreciated!

  Test A is the "stream test" and error 3A is "write while write protected".
The service manual suggests the microprocessor board (big board in the bottom
of the upper drive tray), cables, and host controller. In my experience, this
can also be caused by having the wrong number of bulkhead connectors which
"swap" the cables. Do you get this error with no SDI cables connected to the
drive? If not, look at your cables and make sure there are an even number of
bulkhead connectors and an odd number of SDI cables - it should be:

DRIVE [SDI CABLE2] BULKHEAD [SDI CABLE1] BULKHEAD [SDI CABLE2] CONTROLLER

  where SDI CABLE2 are the cables permanently attached to the drive and con-
troller, and SDI CABLE1 is a normal BC26 SDI cable.

