	We've been using 3600ft tapes on a TU80, (actually, the original
	Cipher drive, not the one redone for DEC,) at 3200bpi for years
	without any problems. (On a PDP11 system however.)

	In general, the only difference is the that the 3600' tapes are
	thinner, and are a little more prone to stretching if your tape
	drive tends to be the Schwartzenneger type. 

	We have seen essentially no difference in performance between
	2400' and 3600', and some of our backups are using humongously long 
	records, (we have a home-brew backup writing 16kbyte or 32. block
	records.)

	I would seriously question that tech's statement, at least until
	they gave me a solid reason why there was a difference.

