the surlus place in my truck, and got the thing. I didn't want to
lay it on its side (might jostle something loose), so I tied it
standing straight up in the truck bed, as far forward as it would go.

  I rocketed back to the office no sweat. Now, I've been pulling into
the parking garage the same way for years, so I don't give it much
thought. As I approached the bottom of the ramp, I noticed something
I didn't usually pay much attention to...a big piece of pipe, hung on
chains across the ramp, with a sign that said MAX Clearance 6'6". Now,
as I sped toward this, I suddenly realized, TU80 + truck bed
height > 6'6"... I slammed on the binders and shouted a dirty word. It
was too late...the TU80 slammed into the pipe with a loud bang. It
rocked back against the ropes, stretching them like rubber bands, then
cannoned forward into the back of the truck bed with another loud bang.
Meanwhile, due to the conservation of energy, the enormous pipe
reached the limit of its swing, and pendulumed back into the TU80
again, repeating the entire cycle of noises, crashes and dirty word
shoutings a few times.

  To make a long story short (I know, too late for that), fools luck
saved me - the TU80 only had a couple of tiny dents on it, and, after
some tense moments worked after I reseated a card in it. The
dent in the back of the truck bed and the crease in my dignity
were much larger...and I now always consider load height when 
