schmidf@iwb.mw.tu-muenchen.de (Frank Schmid) writes:

>I have the following problem:
>I am trying to build up a MAP-MMS comunication between DEComni ULTRIX
>and SISCO MMS-EASE OS2.
>After succesfully haveing established a connection to a remote VMD
>(SISCO-sample-server), the following DEComni function-call fails:

>status = omni_get_remote_attributes(...)

>IOSB-Contents (if attr=omni_c_attr_all) :
> general=801188866 (Length field too large),
> network=0,provider=0

>IOSB-Contents (if attr=omni_c_cls_dom or omni_c_cls_pi or
>omni_c_cls_var_list or omni_c_cls_named_var;) :
>general=80118482 (Association terminated before service completion) ,
>                            network=0,provider=0


>What's going wrong ? 


First, check out what MMS-Version you assigned to the remote VMD
(MMS-EASE). If this is version 0 (Draft IS MMS), then the following
*could* happen: DEComni sends (along with other services) an
Identify.request to MMS-EASE in order to get_the_remote_attributes. Now,
if the MMS-EASE-Server has *more* that 16 characters in any of the
Vendor, Model, or Revision Fields of the Identify.response, which would
be perfectly legal for MMS-IS (Version 1), but not for MMS-DIS (Version
0), then DEComni may complain about that in form of "Length field too
large".

Again, there may be other causes, but I think you should first try to
reduce the number of characters of the MMS-EASE-Server Identification.

Hope that helps!

--
