-- 
Upgrading a 6000-410 to a 420 is (as your FE told you) fairly easy from a
hardware point of view.  There is also a command he should probably execute
to make sure that both board are at the same microcode level.

The big problem you will probably have is with licenses. I don't know what
a "CSLG" license is, but upgrading from a -410 to a -420 requires more units
on all licenses - including the "system integrated products" and VMS licenses.
Also, I have seem some poorly designed 3rd party products that check for
system type as part of their "license check".  You may get bitten if you have
software of this type installed on your system.

Don't forget to update your maintenance contract with DEC to reflect the fact
that you now have a 6000-420 instead of a 6000-410.

