OSF will run fine on the Alpha/PC; OSF/1 on the Alpha PC does support the display.

We don't sell it as a "workstation" as the PC graphics adaptor, while
good for PC's (a Qvision board), is not on the performance curve of engineering
workstations, and don't want to misrepresent it to people coming from the
workstation market, who might expect better graphics performance than any
ISA or EISA based graphics adaptor could provide.  We will obviously
fix this when PCI based Alpha's are available, since PCI's performance
is comparable to TURBOchannel.

Bottom line: most casual users will fine quite acceptable graphics performance,
but "power workstation users" wouldn't...
