To use the audio capability of the 5000/25, you really don't NEED to
install a speaker off the back panel but it may get you higher fidelity.
What you DO need though is the software.  This is freely available from
DEC; they call it AudioFile V2.0 and it is available via ftp at their
Colorado Lab site.  I believe the address is crl.dec.com but don't quote
me :^)

Anyway, you need to get that source and compile and install it.  Reboot
the system to activate the driver.  Once that's done you'll have a few
new commands, one of which is aplay.  Feed aplay a sound file and voila,
you should hear it.  I use it frequently for Internet Talk-Radio files
and other .au files found around the net with only minor problems.  It
seems occasionally to lose track of itself, but replaying the file
usually works.  That behavior is much reduced now that I've moved up to
24MB of memory too.

Once that's going, xmosaic should work although I had some problems with
the showaudio script.  I ended up hacking it down to 1 line with the
aplay command on it!  Has worked fine for every audio file I've listened
to through Mosaic.

Good luck; it's great fun!

Dave Goodwin



