       EDWARD LUCENTE TO ADDRESS "THE OPEN CLIENT/SERVER ADVANTAGE"
                        AT DECUS '93/SAN FRANCISCO

Digital's Vice President, Worldwide Sales And Marketing To Deliver Keynote



Edward Lucente, vice president, Worldwide Sales and Marketing, Digital
Equipment Corporation, will deliver the keynote address at DECUS '93/San
Francisco, which is sponsored by the U.S. Chapter of the Digital Equipment
Computer Users Society (DECUS).  Entitled, "The Open Client/Server
Advantage," the address is scheduled for 8:00 a.m. on Monday, December 6,
at the Moscone Convention Center in San Francisco, site of the weeklong
DECUS event.

Lucente will describe his vision for open client/server computing and the
challenges faced by companies trying to tie their people, business and
technology objectives together for competitive advantage.

"Mr. Lucente is responsible for articulating Digital's business strategies,
and as such, we are very pleased that he will deliver the keynote address
at DECUS '93/San Francisco," said Margaret Knox, president of the DECUS
U.S. Chapter.  "Open client/server computing and information on Digital's
position in this area are essential to the Information Technology
practitioners who make up DECUS.  Recent surveys of our membership revealed
that nearly 90% of DECUS U.S. Chapter members rely on Digital as the
cornerstone vendor for their computing environments which embrace many
different platforms, operating systems and application software.  The
keynote will be timely as DECUS helps its members solve real world,
heterogeneous, multiplatform problems."

DECUS '93/San Francisco is a one-week event featuring in-depth seminars,
technical symposium sessions, a multivendor trade show and the Digital
Technology Center.  The sessions and seminars run December 4 - 10 and the
trade show runs December 7 - 9.  Two new additions this year are an
in-depth spotlight on Windows NT and technology streams on PATHWORKS 5.0
migration, Internet usage and electronic mail.

Participants who register by the early-bird deadline, November 15, will
receive a discount on registration fees.  To register early call
1-800-DECUS55.

DECUS members solve their organizations' computing problems and stay
informed about industry issues and emerging technologies with the aid of
the U.S. Chapter's semiannual national seminars, symposium and trade show
event; regional conferences; local seminars program; Special Interest and
Local Users Groups; electronic conferencing system; and public domain
library.

