Superscalar means the CPU can execute > 1 instruction per clock cycle.  In
particular, here is an excerpt from Motorola "PowerPC Microprocessor Fact
Sheet":

"Superscalar Processor
The PowerPC 601 microprocessor is a superscalar design capable of issuing
and retiring three instructions per clock.  Instructions issue to multiple
executions units, execute in parallel, and can complete out of order, while
preserving program correctness."

