(copied from comp.org.decus, et al.  Sorry for the duplication.)

I'm scheduled to give a two-day seminar on Windows NT kernel-mode device
drivers at the DECUS gathering in San Francisco in December.  (Seminar dates
are Dec. 4 and 5, Sat. and Sun.; the entire "event" is the 4th through the
10th.) 

I'm appending the seminar abstract as it was published in the DECUS
announcements.  Note, I've since decided that I overstated the importance of
VMS driver experience.  The *ideal* prior experience is still VMS driver
experience, since the I/O subsystems (and certain key aspects of the memory
management subsystems) of VMS and NT are so much alike... but the way the
schedule for the two days is shaping up, there should be enough time to cover
the material to everyone's satisfaction. 

BUT... Registration so far has been minimal and so the seminar may be
cancelled.  I really do want to give this (and not because I get paid for it;
I don't!  I get, um, you should pardon the pun, peripheral benefits). 

I'm not expecting anyone to decide to attend based on this note.  But, if you
were interested in this seminar and were thinking in terms of signing up at
the door, you should know that there's a good chance you won't be able to. 
The advance registration deadline is the 15th of November... next Monday.  (I
don't know if that's midnight eastern time or what.  Better play it safe and
assume that it's Monday the 15th, 5 PM Eastern time.)  Folks who get their
registration in by then will help push the seminar over the top. 

If you want to sign up in advance, you still can.  First, fetch the PostScript
versions of the registration and housing forms via anonymous FTP from
decus.org. The directory is decus93-sanfran , and the file names are
reg-form.ps and housing-form.ps .  Next, ... , er, well, maybe this step 
ought to be first:  Get permission from whomever to go!  Anyway, fill out the
registration form and fax it to 1-508-841-3373.  Note that (a) it's two 
sided, and they'll want to receive both sides; (b) you can send in a P.O. 
with it; (c) you can also pay by any of the common credit cards. 

Note also that if you can get immediate approval for the seminar, but
approval for the rest of the week will take longer, you can still sign up
for the seminar in advance, and register on-site for the symposium sessions.
(But that will cost more than registering in advance.)  

Of course, I will mention that there are many other worthy seminars being
offered too... and some of them are similarly "doubtful" due to low reg
counts.  Don't count on being able to sign up on-site! The same anonymous ftp
site has the abstracts for all seminars (and for all sessions during 
Symposium week).  

The deadline for processing hotel reservations through the DECUS housing 
bureau has passed, but the hotels can still be contacted directly, or you can
simply make your own arrangements in the area.  The Symposium proper will be
at the Moscone Convention Center; the seminar may be held there or in one of
the nearby hotels.   The San Francisco Hilton and the San Francisco Marriott
