Regarding the question of "what is a 64-bit quantity called in the
Alpha AXP architecture", the answer really is "quadword".  The fact that the
origin of this term derives from two processor generations previous (PDP-11)
is irrelevant.  It's much less confusing to just coin a term and stick with
it rather than change it each time the word length changes.  Of course, as
others have pointed out, "quadword" is just one possible choice, the one that
Digital has chosen for its own systems, but by all means not the only
choice.
