I'm not familiar with that area of VMS, but as a file systems weenie,
I'll hazard a guess that the changes are often still in an unshared
cache and about to/in the process of going out to disk when the
next process gets the lock and does a read, and what you need to do
is have each process do the equivalent of a UNIX flush (write all
dirty pages to disk) operation (and be sure it completes) before the
process releases the lock.
