The speeds are relative.  From a typical 1 GB SCSI disk you can probably
read at around 2,300 KB/sec.  On a DEC 3000 Model 500 I can read from
memory (the slow way, using dd(1)) at around 47,000 KB/sec.  If I had
to get instructions at that speed to execute, the system would be slow.
Fortunately, there is usually faster cache memory between execution
and memory.

On the original issue of needing 128 MB, it does depend on the
application.  We have 96 MB and 64 MB systems here and for
ordinary work, they're more than fast enough.
