>I am running DEC Pathworks and one of my services is a modem that my users
>share  that is connected to a terminal server (DS200) and my service is via 
>LAT.  I have HP users who run HP Advancelink and need to connect to the modem.
>How can HP Advancelink be configured to recognize the network connection?

We have several year-old versions of AdvanceLink in play and they do not
support connections over anything but a COMx: port.  Your later version may
vary but if your documentation doesn't discuss the possibility then it
just Doesn't Do It.

>Thanks for your help.  If you do not know the answer but can point me in the
>right direction I would appreciate it.  DEC Support Services could not help
>me.

Have you tried talking to HP's Support Services?  After all, AdvanceLink
is an HP product.

Pathworks may also be able to help you through the use of LATCOM (d/l'able
from Compu$erve), which supposedly lets you access a LAT service via a BIOS
operated COMx: port.  But this won't work with AdvanceLink if it addresses
the COMx: UART directly.

Your other option is to give these users Reflection 1, which can use your
existing LAT capability for a connection.
