The ratio is almost a perfect 2x at linpack100x100.  This benchmark fits
entirely within the cache.  The only thing that effects the benchmark is 
the CPU.  You get a 1.5 from clock speed and another 33% from the faster
FPU.  In the case of the other programs, especially the 1000x1000, the 
cache is the more important factor.  You don't just tuck one million
floats into a small cache.  Does that make sense now?

