that run native under Solaris as well as the even larger number of
applications that come from the DOS world that run under one of several x86
emulators and the applications that come from the Windows world and run
under the Windows emulator (WABI).

The truth is, everyone has WABI, everyone has x86 emulation and/or hardware
add-in boards, everyone has NFS, TCP/IP, X, Motif, etc... and all the
hardware runs at pretty much the same speed - some systems are screamers
right now, but they will get displaced with screamer systems that cost less
from other vendors in a few months, ad infinitum.  So, how do you
differentiate your product?  Advertising :-).  My claim thus is that all of
these OS and hardware wars are ultimately pointless if you look at the
bigger computing picture, so why don't we all have fun and tear the crap out
of each other's OSes...?

