Yep, that'll do it.  If mem_space is an integer pointer, as you
indicated, it will be aligned on a 4-byte boundary.  Pointers must be
aligned on 8-byte boundaries to avoid unaligned access problems.  It's
likely that mem_space itself is 8-byte aligned, so that mem_space+1 is
only 4-byte aligned, hence the problems you see.
