>A fine history of hardware and software innovation, products that are a good
>value for the money, and a good company attitude.  We also have a wonderful
>CEO that is capable of seeing market trends and predicting cutomer
>expectations, and will admit when he has made a mistake, rather than trying
>to be dogmatic about a concept until the very end.  I'm not mentioning any
>names here, mind you...  Anyway, why is it that people on the VMS and NT
