Err...  Anyone who's been following my contributions to this thread will
know that I am strongly pro-UNIX, but I had to giggle to hear anyone saying
such things about Sun of all companies.  Especially the bit about a good
company attitude and a visionary CEO.  I had some disagreements with Ken
Olsen's attitudes, but though he was off-base when he called UNIX "snake
oil", McNealy certainly qualifies as a snake oil salesman.  The last really
good thing to come out of Sun was NFS, and even that has needed fixing for
a while.

Sun's position over the past 5 or 6 years has been to take advantage of
the market perception that Sun is an "Open" company to foist thinly
disguised proprietary solutions on unsuspecting customers.  DEC, being
perceived as a proprietary solutions provider, has had to move to true
open solutions.  I remember when your CEO who can see market trends and
predict customer expectations finally said the M word, and it was less
than a year ago, long after DEC and HP had produced Motif for Sun platforms,
and long after customers had moved in droves to the Motif interface.

- Brad
