Here are some hints for getting it to work.  By no means is this a recipe.

1.  Here are my entries in /etc/acucap:
#
#Boca - Hayes compatible smart modem hooked to a pulse only phone.
# See switch setting above.
#
# switches (see above) No Flow Control
boca-p:\
        :db:cr:hu:ls:ss=ATZ0\r\d:sr=OK:sd#250000:\
        :di=AT&q5s36=7s48=128&d2&c1&K0M0DP:dt=,\r,:\
        :dd#50000:fd#40:rs=,:os=CONNECT:ds=\d+++\dATZ\r:ab=\d+++\dATZ:
# switches as boca-p but tone dialing
boca:\
        :cr:hu:ls:ss=ATZ0\r\d:sr=OK:sd#250000:di=AT&K0M0DT:dt=,\r,:\
        :dd#50000:fd#40:rs=,:os=CONNECT:ds=\d+++\dATZ\r:ab=\d+++\dATZ:

2.  Here are some of my entries in /etc/remote:  (see man remote)
# Locally know remote systems
#
boca:pa=none:br#19200:dv=/dev/tty00:
orph22:pa=none:br#19200:du:pn=@:dv=/dev/ttyd0:at=boca-p:

3.  I did a 'chmod +rw /dev/tty00' and 'chmod +rw /dev/ttyd0'


