      DIGITAL INTRODUCES INDUSTRY'S HIGHEST CAPACITY 5.25-INCH
           SOLID-STATE DISK WITH INTEGRATED DATA RETENTION


       Continues Push Towards Leadership in the $250 Million*
                       Solid-State Disk Market


MAYNARD, Mass. -- November 3, 1993 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced the industry's highest capacity 5.25-inch form 
factor solid-state disk with integrated data retention.  The ESP580 
solid-state disk boasts 856 MB of storage capacity, near-
instantaneous access time, and a Fast SCSI-2 single-ended interface.  
Its sophisticated integrated data retention system provides the same
non-volatility as magnetic drives.  The ESP580 product joins 
Digital's rapidly growing family of low-cost, plug-and-play 
solid-state disks, which enhance system performance by providing 
unparalleled access speed to frequently used files. 
     "There is a growing market opportunity for solid-state disks 
because they're the best solution for reliable, fast I/O 
performance.  Solid-state disks offer the same fast access to data 
regardless of whether you are performing reads or writes," said Jack 
Sharp, business manager of Digital's Storage Business Unit.  "We are 
seeing more Digital solid-state disks used in systems running time-
sensitive, mission-critical applications, and believe they will
play a larger role over time in the storage solutions market." 

     "Digital's solid-state disks are designed to increase system 
performance by providing high-speed I/O to match today's accelerated 
CPU speeds," said Madeline Flynn, Digital's solid-state disk 
marketing manager.  "By placing the most frequently accessed files 
on solid-state disks, while reserving magnetic disks for less active 
files, the system is able to complete more transactions per second." 
     The ESP580 disk provides a near-instantaneous access speed of 
less than 1 millisecond (ms), which offers dramatic advantages over 
the approximately 10 ms access speed of conventional magnetic disks, 
and can execute more than 800 I/Os per second.  In addition, the 
sophisticated data retention system fully protects applications' 
mission critical information by continuously copying data from its 
solid-state arrays to an internal hard drive.  In the event of a 
power outage or system failure, data is fully protected. 
     Like all Digital's solid-state disks, the ESP580 solution 
leverages several advanced technologies to lead the industry in 
performance.  The disk 'plugs and plays' in standard storage slots 
in systems and storage arrays, so it does not require special 
packaging or installation. And, because it is software-compatible 
with magnetic disks, no operating system or application changes are
needed.  In addition, technologies such as power-up diagnostics, 
Reed Solomon error correction code (ECC), VLSI components, bad block 
replacement, and firmware, ensure data reliability and security at a 
low cost. 


Applications
     The ESP580 solid-state disks are designed to improve system 
performance for high-value, data processing applications.  These 
