               DIGITAL JOINS "FAST ETHERNET ALLIANCE"



MAYNARD, Mass. -- November 5, 1993 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced its membership in the Fast Ethernet Alliance (FEA).  
The FEA is one of two multivendor consortiums dedicated to 
developing specifications for a high-speed 100 megabit per second 
Ethernet standard-based upon the core Ethernet technology pioneered 
by Digital, Intel and others.  
     "Digital's commitment to provide total interoperability through 
open systems makes it imperative that we be active in 
standards-based extensions of Ethernet performance.  That's why we 
joined the FEA," commented William L. Maro, group manager, Network 
Interconnect Product Group. "At the same time, we continue to work 
with 100Base-VG vendors and participate in both the FEA and 
100Base-VG work groups."
     The FEA is a 15-member consortium and includes 3Com 
Corporation, Grand Junction Networks, Intel Corporation, National 
Semiconductor, Sun Microsystems Computer Corporation, SynOptics 
Communications, Inc. and others.  It has presented a high-speed 
Ethernet specification called 100BASE-X to an industry standards 
organization, the Institute of Electrical and Electronic Engineers 
(IEEE) standards committees, for consideration.

     According to Karl Pieper, Digital's High-Speed Networks Program 
manager, "Digital's goal is to deliver high-speed networking to the 
desktop at the best price/performance levels in the industry.  To 
support that effort we will continue to evaluate high-performance 
technologies and participate in those forums that can best 
contribute to achieving that goal."
