This problem is always present with SCSI compatible disks ...
this summer we bought quite a lot of these (5 or 6 don't remember ...)
some are for VAXes others for Suns, SGIs, DECstations and AXPs ....
some works as expected some don't

examples: 
 - on a Sparc station, the disk forced the SCSI bus to SLOW scsi
 - one works on VAXes and AXPs but not on SGIs 
 - etc ...

The problem is with the SCSI protocol. Some commands and their answers are
fully specified, some aren't
a compatible disk is *quite* always seen in console mode ...
but the operating system is sometimes "compatible blind"

here, we asked our vendor for "a 2Gb SCSI drive for a *machine*"
if THAT drive doesn't work on THAT machine, he (the vendor) have to change
that drive  ... I don't know an other solution, Sorry

