One of my more unpleasant tasks is trying to keep the keyboards here clean.
Primarily, we use Wyse WY85's and the keycaps come off fairly easily. I just
take 'em all off and dump them in a mixture of Spray-9 (tm) and hot water.
Swish them around for a minute and they come up like new. 

While the caps are off, I shake the keyboards upside down and get all the 
potato chip and cookie crumbs out of them too.

One of the programmers once complained that his keyboard was broke - every 
time he hit the e key, the r and 4 characters would appear on the screen too.
I took a look at it, and there was a gob of some sticky stuff glueing the 
keys together :-)

And then there is the nail polish on the keys from the data entry girls...

