Date: Wed, 3 Nov 1993 12:37:37 GMT

We recently installed some second-hand DECSERVER 100 terminal servers. They
work fine, but we encountered a problem when our system re-boots after a power
failure. Our other servers (DECSERVER 300s) resume operation as soon as the
computer is back up, but the 100s aren't online until about 15 minutes later.

We suspect that part of the problem is that our computer (VAX 6320) has a
timer connected to it that forces a 3-minute delay in restoring power after an
electrical failure. This means that when power is restored to the servers,
and they attempt to download the software from the VAX, they get no response.
I know that when this occurs with the DECSERVER 300, the delay time between
successive attempts gets longer and longer; this may be happening here, as
well, but the delay is far too long.

As a test, we tried plugging in a spare DECSERVER 100, but not connecting it to
the DELNI until about 15 minutes later. We saw the same phenomenon - the server
didn't come online for another 10-15 minutes. On the other hand, when the
server was connected to the DELNI, and momentarily unplugged from the
electrical outlet - it came back online immediately; i.e., there was no delay
in downloading the software.

Is there some configuration parameter that affects the delay time?
Unfortunately, we have no documentation for these servers.

Any help you can offer would be greatly appreciated.

