Oh, ultrix certainly could be ported to the Alpha, but there are good
reasons that DEC didn't do so.  Firstly, it's USL/Univel-encumbered,
and I would imagine that DEC's licensing arrangement with the OSF is
far more favorable.  They also keep themselves from being subject to
Ray Noorda's whims...  Further, the kernel design of Ultrix is not
very conducive to multiprocessor implementations, whereas that of
OSF/1 is.  Finally, OSF/1 preserves virtually all of the likeable
features of Ultrix and introduces some very valuable new ones.  After
setting up some Alphas and porting quite a bit of code from Ultrix to
OSF/1, I must say that, in terms of system administration, the
learning curve from Ultrix to OSF/1 is almost nonexistant and that I
have yet to run across software, barring that that is extremenly
hardware dependent that doesn't port with an absolute minimum of work.
Going from Ultrix to OSF/1 is no worse than, and in some ways better
than, going from one major release of Ultrix to another.
-ben
