	Soap and water do wonders. Anything stronger can be a real bummer.
	As an example, I have heard several people describe finding out the
	hard way that mixing sugary stuff, (like Coke,) and alcohol, (often
	considered the universal cleaner in medical environments,) results
	in a compound that is a fairly effective glue.

