The Fall 1993 U.S. Chapter DECUS Symposium is being held December 6-10 at the
Moscone Convention Center, San Francisco, California.  If you are planning to
attend the Symposium, we ask that you consider volunteering to chair one or
more sessions.

If you have never chaired a session before, DECUS offers a short training
session Sunday evening.  Chairing a session is easy, and guarantees you a good
seat in the room!  So if you know you are going to attend a particular Windows
NT session, please consider chairing it as well.

Attached is a list of sessions in the special Windows NT track.  To volunteer
to chair a session, please list the session code and title, along with your
name, phone, and postal address, and e-mail that information to
JOSLIN@DECUS.ORG.  (You can simply reply to this article, in fact.)  We need
to receive your list of requested sessions no later than November 26th.

Sessions will be assigned on a first-come/first-serve basis.  You will receive
a follow-up e-mail message shortly before the Symposium indicating which
sessions have been assigned to which volunteer.

Should you require more detailed information about a session than the title
listed below, you can consult the gopher server at cerritos.edu, specifying
the session code as the search string.  Session abstracts are also available
via anonymous ftp at decus.org, or via mail server (send single-word message
HELP to address mailserv@decus.org).  An interactive search and query facility
is available via telnet to decus.org, username decusprogram.

Thanks in advance!

