In article <1993Nov9.141914.1@matai.vuw.ac.nz> Andrew.Greer@vuw.ac.nz writes:
>
>  Hi,
>     We are looking at moving from Ultrix on a DECsystem 5400 to DEC OSF/1 on a
>DEC 3000-300. One of the questions we have is there any memory usage increase
>in going from the DECsystem to the Alpha system. Both the current machine and
>the new machine have 64MB, is this likely to be a problem on the Alpha. Does
>anyone have experiences of this sort of 'upgrade' that they can share?


You will probably win overall in terms of memory usage, due to the
sharable libraries in OSF.  There may be a minor increase in memory
due to some things like pointers being longer.

In general, the move is a no-brainer.  Many binaries will run as is;
some will just need recompilation; some will need a minor edit to a makefile
(the standard libraries are in a different place); if the code has been
doing bad things in terms of assumptions about size, lint -Q will tell
you about most of those assumptions.

DEC has a porting guide which I think you can get a copy of
(sorry, I don't know its order number.)  You can also log into the
publically available DEC Alpha system and experiment.

