Subject: Rounding double precision numbers
Keywords: rounding
Message-ID: <910@lax.lax.pe-nelson.com>
Date: 9 Nov 93 22:01:17 GMT
Followup-To: comp.lang.c
Organization: PE-Nelson
Lines: 22


We are trying to find routines for VMS which will allow double
precision numbers to be rounded in a controlled manner.  

Specifically if the number is exactly 'n.5' the rounding must be to
the nearest even integer.  For example, 3.5 would round to 4 while 2.5
would round to 2.  This is quite easy under SunOS, using irint() to
round the number and the ieee_flags() to set the rounding direction,
both defined in math.h.  All of the include files involved, with
SunOS, contain a Sun copyright.

Are these ieee routines a standard?  If so, who defines it and more
importantly are there implementations around which could run under
VMS.

Incidentally, DEC support claims that neither OSF/1 nor Ultrix contain
these routines.


-- 

-- Milt


