Calling C from FORTRAN and vice versa should not necessarily cause you problems on the Alpha. One possibility could be that you are mixing floating point
and double precision addresses. Recall that with ANSI C, given

void test(x)
float x;
{
}

then x must be aligned on a double word boundary but with

void test(float x)
{
}

then x can be aligned on a single word boundary. (To my mind this is a screw-up
with ANSI C, but that's a different issue...)

