In <2bjs95$lsq@harbinger.cc.monash.edu.au> andrew@daneel.rdt.monash.edu.au (Andrew Moore) writes:

> I want to add an rz28 to a 5000/120 running 4.3 and  in the not too
> distant future 4.3A

> Talking to the local sales digit, I am told the 2Gig rz28's are not
> supported on the DECStations.

As noted here by others, the fact that it's not supported doesn't mean
it won't work, just that DEC won't guarantee it or help you resolve problems
under normal maintenance agreements.  The "support" can differ between
different machines at the same OS level.

DEC likes to say that the SPD for an OS is _the_ statement of what devices
are supported, but I know that on occasions devices do get official support
added later.


> Appart from being the sign of things to come, I was wondering apart
> from the lack of a disktab entry what other things need to be made
> happen for this to be a happy marrage ?

You will need to modify /sys/data/cam_data.c to let the system recognise
the disk and make correct assumptions about buffering, etc.  This assumes
that you use CAM (it's optional before 4.3A).  If you're not using CAM on
4.3 my advice is to start.  It won't affect any applications, and it's
much better than the old SCSI drivers.

Note that /sys/data/cam_data.c is revision specific, so you will need to
re-apply changes when you move OS.  I have to maintain different versions
for 4.2A, 4.3, and 4.3A at the moment (my changes have been for better
Exabyte "support").
