|>>> Pointers must be
|>>> aligned on 8-byte boundaries to avoid unaligned access problems.
|>> 
|>> Let me rephrase that to make sure it's not misleading.  _Storage_ for
|>> pointers must be aligned on 8-byte boundaries.  To avoid unaligned
|>> access problems, pointer _values_ need to be aligned to the natural
|>> alignment of the item to which they point.
