This is what Bill Zaharchuk (zaharchuk@harbor.enet.dec.com)
answered precisely my question,
and he did it in less than 20 hours,
really good service over there (by the way, where is
harbor.enet.dec.com physically spoken). So here the news:

The Model 300 uses SIMMs that are either 8MB or 32MB in capacity
added in pairs. There are up to 4-pairs of SIMMs used in a Model 300
system. You currently have 2-pairs of 8MB SIMMs (4 x 8MB) used to
get 32MB. The SIMMs are standard 72pin, parity memory @ 70nsec.

I know that our MS16 parts have been tested and you should 
make sure you get the same level of service from a 3rd party
if you choose that source.

The only rule is if you use 32MB SIMMs, they must be installed
in the first slots, ahead of the 8MB SIMMs. If you forget
this, the memory sniffer will see the 8MB SIMMs first, and
than think all the SIMMs are 8MB, including your 32MB SIMMs.

Thanks again


