fat84@cc.usu.edu (Dave Roberts) asks:

>   2) how to configure a dummy cable to fool the VAX into thinking
>      that a keyboard is attached (which pins to cross, etc.)?


This appears to be a pretty common question.  The normal way is to
attach a cable such as the BCC05 to the 9-pin printer port connection.
The cable has been around since the PRO350 days and is labeled with
"Console" on it.

To make one of these cables, short pins 8 and 9.  The layout of the
pins should be:

PIN	SIGNAL				EIA RS232

1	Protective Ground		AA
2	Transmit Data			BA
3	Receive Data			BB
4
5	Data Terminal Ready		CD
6	Data Set Ready			CC
7	Signal Ground			AB
8	Ground
9	Terminal L

This should cause the system to boot using the serial line as the
console. 

