	Just as a follow on note, I just cleaned a DEC keyboard that had a 
coke spilled into it. It of course was allowed to dry so that the keys stuck 
and was not very usefull.

	Being very dirty I took it appart and washed the case in warm soapy 
water until clean. I taped over the beeper (I would remove a speaker if there 
were one for this next step) on the keybpard PCB and placed the whole unit 
into a bathtub full of warm soapy water. Then using a stiff brush I scrubbed 
away at the key faces. Follow with a good rinse. The keys came clean, the coke
was washed away and all came clean. This next step is very important. I then 
placed the PCB over a heater vent over night to dry and remove any absorbed 
moisture.

	The bottem line. It is not for the faint of heart, Best for a spilled 
on and otherwise lost keyboard. And, It works.


