I (personally) don't think you really want to do this.  If it was 
customizable, there wouldn't be anything preventing spoofing of 
identification strings.  As the identification strings are used for ALF and 
often used by security administrators to determine the source of failed 
login or breakin attempts, allowing a user to change their identification 
string at will can hamper efforts to find the user.

But DEC added the ability to remove password histories when you delete a 
user in VMS V6.0 (which, IMO, is a security risk), so they probably allow a 
user to change their identification string on the VXT2000 .....   sigh.

