The R80 is an SMD drive (at least, the one I have to climb over to get into my
room certainly is). The RB730 is a combined SMD and RL-series controller that
was integrated into the VAX 11/730 CPU, and could not easily be used with
anything else.
The R80 has 3 boards in the logic assembly - a servo board, a CPU board and a
personality board. The HDA is certainly the same between the RA80 and the R80,
and I suspect the RM80 is the same as well.
Also, I think that the personality board was replaced between different
versions of the drive, and that a drive with _no_ personality board will fail
hardcore diagnostics (a serious DEC name according to the service guide) and is
certainly not SMD

