But the context in which you made your statement was of using a control-Y to
get a DCL prompt, then spawning another process and continuing the original. 
Now you tell us that you weren't bothering to spawn the command.  A given
process can only run images sequentially.  If you activate a second image, the
original image is run down before the second one is activated.  The only
commands you can use without causing image rundown are callbacks to the CLI.

