The bulk of VMS was written in VAX Macro and Bliss, and the AXP version is
still written in those two languages, at least for the time being.  The
introduction of a new Bliss compiler and the change from a macro assembler
to a macro compiler allowed this.

I have heard that DEC intends to start using C, but I don't think the plan is
to rewrite things for the sake of rewriting them.  As components are changed
for other reasons, such as functionality changes, they may be converted to C.

DEC has definitely said that device drivers will be written in C in the future.
Many of the internal entry points will be changed from a JSB interface to a
CALLX interface to support high level languages.

