In article <1993Nov1.193133.26311@newsgate.sps.mot.com>, wolfson@sps.mot.com writes...
>I've recently aquired my very own PDP 11/34 and 4 RK06 Disk drives.
> 
> 
>What is the size of the RK06 packs (10Mb? 16MB?).  

About 13.5Mbyte. Each pack contains 2 platters, with a total of 3 data surfaces
and 1 servo surface.

> 
>I also need a good source for Parts.  What I particularly need are the drive
>to CPU cables, the cables were cut apparently because someone didn't want to take
>the time to figure out how to remove them.  Do I really need the external cables
>or can I just extend the internal ribbon cables?

Ouch!. OK, The drive cables consist of the following
1) A 40 pin ribbon cable from one of the boards in the RK611 controller to a
bulkhead transition connector (a little black thing, often bolted to the rear
of  the CPU rack). This is a plain ribbon cable
2) A round cable, with zero insertion force plugs between this transistion
connector and a similar connector on the backplane of the first drive. It
connects to port A in (assuming your drives have the interface card in the
normal slot).
3) Identical round cables between the port A out connector of one drive to port
A in of the next
4) A terminator plug in the port A out socket of the last drive.

If you are very lucky, you will find transition connectors in the stands of
each drive. In this case, you can ignore them, and use the round cables that
link the drive to it's transition connector as a drive interconnect cable. You
can't connect ribbon cables directly to the drives, as the connectors don't
fit. However, if you have the connectors off the cut cables, you can make a
straight-through cable using twisted pair cable, and link up the drives with
that. The 2 pins on the same horizontal row of the plug are the differential
pair for each signal, and should be linked with the wires of a tiwsted pair in
the cable. I seem to remember that one of the corner pins is a +5V power for
the terminator, and should NOT be linked.

All you need is the cables described above. If you some arrangement with cable
connectors in the stand for each drive, ignore it, and use the cables to
implement the above scheme.

